{"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"themselves.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance"],"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides"}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Replacing a hand-written registry","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}]},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registry is a list someone has to keep in step with the code: every analytics event type in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, every route in a table, every dependency registered in one function at startup. A new type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that isn’t added works everywhere except where the list is read, and nothing tells you. Moving the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list onto LinkerSets takes four steps, and the list is deleted at the end."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Take an analytics library whose events are types conforming to "},{"code":"AnalyticsEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", collected by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hand so the library can validate their schemas at launch:"}]},{"code":["public protocol AnalyticsEvent {","    static var name: String { get }","}","","\/\/ Every module's events, listed by hand.","let allEvents: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] = [","    Login.self,","    Logout.self,","    PurchaseCompleted.self,","]"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"1. Give the library a macro","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"1-Give-the-library-a-macro"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Pick a kind (“evnt” is ","type":"text"},{"code":"0x6576_6E74","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind"},{"text":" explains) and add a compiler plugin","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose macro requires the protocol, so its records hold ","type":"text"},{"code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Analytics.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The library declares the macro and the kind, re-exports LinkerSets for the expansion, and reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the set for its users:"}]},{"code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let events = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x6576_6E74)  \/\/ \"evnt\"","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"AnalyticsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")","","public enum AnalyticsEvents {","    public static var all: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] {","        LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The re-export is required. The expansion lands in each user’s file and calls LinkerSets’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#linkerSetRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" there, so that file must see the LinkerSets module. A library that imports"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"LinkerSets without re-exporting it leaves its users’ files failing with “no macro named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"‘linkerSetRecord’” unless each one imports LinkerSets too. The re-export also puts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetKind"},{"type":"text","text":" in scope wherever the library is imported. Keep the kind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internal and hand users the values through the library’s own API ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsEvents.all"},{"type":"text","text":"), so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"set is read in one place."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The LinkerSetsMacroSupport module’s documentation has the package targets this needs.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"2. Read the set beside the list","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"2-Read-the-set-beside-the-list"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Before touching any event, read both and compare them, in a test or a debug build:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let discovered = AnalyticsEvents.all","let missing = allEvents.filter { listed in !discovered.contains { $0 == listed } }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing"},{"type":"text","text":" starts as the whole list and shrinks as events are marked."}]},{"text":"3. Mark each event where it’s declared","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"3-Mark-each-event-where-its-declared"},{"code":["@Event","struct Login: AnalyticsEvent {","    static let name = \"login\"","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event that doesn’t conform fails to compile. A generic event type, or one nested in a generic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type, is refused with a message, as "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" lists; such a type needs its concrete"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specializations listed by hand, or a concrete wrapper."}]},{"text":"4. Delete the list","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"4-Delete-the-list"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty, the library reads the set instead:"}]},{"code":["let allEvents = LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and the hand-written array goes. A new event is registered by writing "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on it, in whichever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module declares it."}]},{"text":"Other registries","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Other-registries"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The same steps fit any list whose entries can be declared as constants, functions or types:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Routes","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"@Route static let profile = Route(path: \"\/profile\")","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", read as "},{"code":"LinkerSet<Route>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Migrations","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"@Migration static func addUsers(_ db: inout Database)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", read as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"LinkerSet<(inout Database) -> Void>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", sorted by a version the migration declares."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Dependency registrations","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Registration static func register(_ container: Container)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"module registering its own factories, read and called once at startup.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A registry whose order matters gets it from the entries, never from the set: the linker’s order is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stable but not one you choose (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":").","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry"]}],"references":{"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSet":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkerset","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every record of one kind, across every image the program has loaded, and the values they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produce."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSet"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSet"}],"title":"LinkerSet","kind":"symbol"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse","kind":"article","title":"What the macros refuse"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/UniqueKeys":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/uniquekeys","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Make two records of one kind with the same key fail to build, within one executable or library."}],"role":"article","title":"Unique keys","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/UniqueKeys"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/DeclaringAKind":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind","title":"Declaring a kind","kind":"article"},"doc://LinkerSetsRuntime/documentation/LinkerSetsRuntime/LinkerSetKind":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersetsruntime\/linkersetkind","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tag that says which client a linker-set record belongs to."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetKind"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"LinkerSetKind"}],"title":"LinkerSetKind","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSetKind"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/Performance":{"role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What records cost as an app grows: nothing at launch, a walk of the records when a set is read,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a few milliseconds of build time per marked declaration."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/performance","kind":"article","title":"Performance"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords","abstract":[{"text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","title":"Finding records","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"role":"collection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets","title":"LinkerSets","kind":"symbol"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"role":"article","title":"Platforms and linking","kind":"article"}}}